    "# PCA on forms of capital in the Younger Bronze Age (1100-500 BCE)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Episode:** `discoverybench:test/archaeology/metadata_19.json/0/0`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question:** *In the PCA on the forms of capital analysed in hundred-year time slices, during the Younger Bronze Age (1100-500 BCE), how does the PC1 value at the beginning of the period at 1100 BCE differ from the subsequent time horizons between 1000 to 500 BCE?*\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:** `data/capital.csv` (39 rows x 12 Z-valued capital features, 100-year slices spanning 4300-500 BCE).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pipeline:**\n",
    "1. Load + parse European-comma decimals, drop meta columns.\n",
    "2. Standardise (mean=0, std=1).\n",
    "3. PCA via `numpy.linalg.eigh` on the covariance matrix.\n",
    "4. Project YBA rows; compare 1100 BCE vs 1000-500 BCE on PC1.\n",
    "5. Robustness: (a) raw covariance; (b) drop ZSichel/ZKeform; (c) PCA fit on YBA-only.\n"
   ]
